			"notes": "Improved Inventory Tabs for **Minecraft 26.3, 26.2, 1.21.1, and 1.20.1** — pick the jar matching your Minecraft version and loader:\n\n| Minecraft | Fabric | NeoForge | Forge |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 26.3 | `…-fabric-26.3-1.5.0.jar` | — (see below) | — |\n| 26.2 | `…-fabric-26.2-1.5.0.jar` | `…-neoforge-26.2-1.5.0.jar` | — |\n| 1.21.1 | `…-fabric-1.21.1-1.5.0.jar` | `…-neoforge-1.21.1-1.5.0.jar` | — |\n| 1.20.1 | `…-fabric-1.20.1-1.5.0.jar` | — | `…-forge-1.20.1-1.5.0.jar` |\n\n## Requirements\n- **All versions**: [Cloth Config](https://modrinth.com/mod/cloth-config). For 26.3 you need Cloth Config **26.3.158 or newer**; on CurseForge it is currently listed under the 26.3 snapshot tag.\n- **Fabric**: Fabric Loader + [Fabric API](https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-api) (Mod Menu recommended for the config button)\n- Java: 25 (MC 26.3 and 26.2) / 21 (MC 1.21.1) / 17 (MC 1.20.1)\n\n## New\n- **Minecraft 26.3 support (Fabric).** 26.3 swapped GLFW for SDL underneath, which changed the key and mouse-button codes; the mod now uses the named input APIs so tabs open, click and page correctly on 26.3. **NeoForge for 26.3 will follow as soon as NeoForge itself publishes a 26.3 build.**\n\n## Fixed\n- The 26.2 Fabric jar could be installed on 26.3, where it crashed on the missing GLFW classes. It is now bounded to 26.2.x; use the 26.3 jar on 26.3."
		},
