			"notes": "Improved Inventory Tabs for **Minecraft 26.2, 1.21.1, and 1.20.1** — pick the jar matching your Minecraft version and loader:\n\n| Minecraft | Fabric | NeoForge | Forge |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 26.2 | `…-fabric-26.2-1.4.3.jar` | `…-neoforge-26.2-1.4.3.jar` | — |\n| 1.21.1 | `…-fabric-1.21.1-1.4.3.jar` | `…-neoforge-1.21.1-1.4.3.jar` | — |\n| 1.20.1 | `…-fabric-1.20.1-1.4.3.jar` | — | `…-forge-1.20.1-1.4.3.jar` |\n\n## Requirements\n- **All versions**: [Cloth Config](https://modrinth.com/mod/cloth-config)\n- **Fabric**: Fabric Loader + [Fabric API](https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-api) (Mod Menu recommended for the config button)\n- Java: 25 (MC 26.2) / 21 (MC 1.21.1) / 17 (MC 1.20.1)\n\n## Fixed\n- **Curios** compatibility: Curios' inventory screen paints its slot panel left of the container, and the left tab column landed on top of it. On Curios screens the tabs now use the right column only, with the page arrows at the top and bottom of that column. This is built in, so no config change is needed. Curios is never referenced directly, so nothing changes when it isn't installed.\n\n## Changed\n- Entries in **Do not show tabs on these screens** now also match a screen's interfaces, not just its class and parent classes."
		},
