			"notes": "Hotfix for 1.4.0. Improved Inventory Tabs for **Minecraft 26.2, 1.21.1, and 1.20.1** — pick the jar matching your Minecraft version and loader:\n\n| Minecraft | Fabric | NeoForge | Forge |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 26.2 | `…-fabric-26.2-1.4.1.jar` | `…-neoforge-26.2-1.4.1.jar` | — |\n| 1.21.1 | `…-fabric-1.21.1-1.4.1.jar` | `…-neoforge-1.21.1-1.4.1.jar` | — |\n| 1.20.1 | `…-fabric-1.20.1-1.4.1.jar` | — | `…-forge-1.20.1-1.4.1.jar` |\n\n## Requirements\n- **All versions**: [Cloth Config](https://modrinth.com/mod/cloth-config)\n- **Fabric**: Fabric Loader + [Fabric API](https://modrinth.com/mod/fabric-api) (Mod Menu recommended for the config button)\n- Java: 25 (MC 26.2) / 21 (MC 1.21.1) / 17 (MC 1.20.1)\n\n## Fixed\n- **fastpipes** and **Create** compatibility: the 1.4.0 \"only blocks with an inventory or menu\" rule hid the tab for blocks that open their screen without a container block entity — the fastpipes **terminal** and Create's **stock ticker**. They always get a tab again. fastpipes pipe segments were already hidden by 1.4.0, since they have nothing to open. If you meet another block whose tab went missing in 1.4.0, add it under **Force show** in the config."
